theo-pod (t-169): keep quantized values within the inverse quantiser's range

unpack_idx_esc() reads escape prefixes with no bound: a run of ones (a
corrupt stream, or the zero bits returned past the end of the buffer) makes
N grow past 32, getbits() shifts by a negative amount and the escaped value
overflows. ISO/IEC 14496-3 allows at most 8 prefix ones (N <= 12, values
below 8192); the prefix loop now stops there. pulse_nc() adds up to 15 to
an escaped value; the sum is clamped to 8191. Larger values index
inverseQuantTable[] (1025 entries, inputs below 8192) past its end in
esc_iquant_scaling(). Found by the host fuzzer (UBSan shift exponent in
getbits.h from unpack_idx_esc, ASan global-buffer-overflow in
esc_iquant_scaling); regression input
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-unbounded-escape.bin.

